  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "2 Chronicles",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 33,
    "summary": "Manasseh reigns in wickedness and worships false gods—He is taken captive into Assyria—He repents and serves the Lord—Amon reigns in unrighteousness and is slain.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Manasseh was twelve years old when he began to reign, and he reigned fifty and five years in Jerusalem:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 21:1 (1–9)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 33:1",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "But did that which was evil in the sight of the Lord, like unto the abominations of the heathen, whom the Lord had cast out before the children of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 22
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 33:2",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For he built again the high places which Hezekiah his father had broken down, and he reared up altars for Baalim, and made groves, and worshipped all the host of heaven, and served them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "2 Chr. 34:3 (3–7)."
          },
          {
            "start": 106,
            "end": 112,
            "text": "Jer. 9:14."
          },
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 129,
            "text": "HEB asheroth —fertility worship symbols."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Jer. 9:14.",
            "prettyString": "Jeremiah 9:14",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "jeremiah",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 14,
                        "end": 14
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 33:3",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Also he built altars in the house of the Lord, whereof the Lord had said, In Jerusalem shall my name be for ever.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 33:4",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And he built altars for all the host of heaven in the two courts of the house of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Chronicles 33:5",
        "book": "2 Chronicles",
        "chapter": 33,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And he caused his children to pass through the fire in the valley of the son of Hinnom: also he observed times, and used enchantments, and used witchcraft, and dealt with a familiar spirit, and with wizards: he wrought much evil in the sight of the Lord, to provoke him to anger.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 51,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 21:6; 2 Chr. 28:3; Ezek. 20:26."
          },
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 110,
            "text": "IE practiced soothsaying."
          },
          {
            "start": 144,
            "end": 154,
            "text": "Deut. 18:12 (10–14)."
          },
          {
            "start": 160,
            "end": 165,
            "text": "IE practiced spiritualism."
          },
          {
            "start": 173,
            "end": 188,
            "text": "TG Spirits, Evil or Unclean."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 21:6; 2 Chr. 28:3; Ezek. 20:26.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 21:6; 2 Chronicles 28:3; Ezekiel 20:26",
